  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"7a\"><p><strong>7a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(2.5)(5.0) + (-v)(0.80) = (2.5 + 0.80)(1.2)\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v \\approx 10.7 \\approx 11\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p>Calculated answer must be given to at least 3 significant figures in order to earn the final mark.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"7b\"><p><strong>7b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Total kinetic energy before collision:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}(2.5)(5.0)^{2} + \\frac{1}{2}(0.80)(10.7)^{2} \\approx 77\"></span> J</p>\n<p>Total kinetic energy after collision:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}(2.5 + 0.80)(1.2)^{2} \\approx 2.4\"></span> J</p>\n<p>Since <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"77&gt;2.4\"></span>, the collision is inelastic.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"7c\"><p><strong>7c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{ave} = \\frac{\\Delta p}{\\Delta t} = \\frac{(3.3)(-0.70) - (3.3)(1.2)}{0.085} \\approx -74\"></span> N</p>\n<p>So the magnitude of the force exerted by the wall on the objects is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"74\"></span> N</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two objects, A and B, are moving towards each other at constant speed on a horizontal, frictionless surface as shown on the diagram. The mass of object A is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5\"></span> kg and its speed is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. The mass of object B is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80\"></span> kg and its speed is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The objects collide, stick together and move to the right at a speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.2\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>a. Show that <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> is about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"11\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>b. Show that the collision is inelastic.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>\n<p>The objects collide with a vertical wall and rebound with a speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.70\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. The objects are in contact with the wall during <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"85\"></span> ms.</p>\n<p>c. Calculate the magnitude of the average force exerted by the wall on the objects.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>"
  },
